WEBVTT

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:05.170
Hey, you! What are you doing over there?

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:09.110
Is either Kondou-san or Hijikata-san in?

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.410
Huh? Y-yeah...

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.640
I think they’re probably inside.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:18.450
The swords are on his right...?

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:19.970
Could you inform them of my arrival?

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.000
Uh, what’s your name?

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:26.220
Hajime... Saito.

00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:00.300
Saito?! If it isn’t Saito!

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:05.720
It has been a long time, Hijikata-san.

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:10.260
Jeez, it’s been forever!

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:14.190
I was worried since you suddenly
stopped coming to the dojo.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:19.200
That was... I apologize
for having worried you.

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:21.470
There’s not need to stand on ceremony!

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:23.020
I swear you haven’t changed...

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:25.830
Well, come on in!

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:27.540
If I may...

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:32.840
But seriously, I’m
amazed you found me here!

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:36.800
I had heard that you were
involved with the Roshigumi...

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:43.310
Even Hijikata-san smiles sometimes, huh?

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:48.850
LED BY DESTINY

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:51.170
You’d like to join the Roshigumi...?

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:51.850
Correct.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:56.870
Although I appreciate the offer,
are you aware of our current situation?

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:58.470
No, I am mostly in the dark.

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:00.860
Well, put simply,

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:04.510
the Roshigumi’s central figure is a
guy named Serizawa, not Kondou-san.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:09.060
We haven’t received an
official appointment or any funding.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:11.720
Even if we stay in Kyoto,
we lack a patron.

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:15.130
In short, we’re in dire straights.

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:16.250
I see.

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:19.690
Despite all that, will you join us?

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:20.760
But of course.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:26.510
Saito, I won’t ask for
the details as to why you

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:27.770
quit visiting the Shieikan.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:31.770
But I at least want to
know what brought you here.

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:34.770
To return the favor.

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:39.780
There is no time save for now
to repay you and Kondou-san

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:43.480
for the kindness you showed me in Edo.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:44.780
That is how I feel.

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:50.460
I see. Right now we need
every reliable ally we can get.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:52.040
I’ll be counting on you!

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:54.240
I offer what little help I can...

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:57.450
By the way, have you run
into the others yet?

00:03:57.830 --> 00:03:59.050
The others?

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:02.550
The guys from the Shieikan, of course!

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:04.940
Are they here as well?

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:05.800
Yeah!

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:09.560
There’s Sannan-san, Souji,
Shinpachi and Harada!

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:12.080
Heisuke and Gen-san are
here with us as well.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:16.300
I thought it was unusual to hear
Hijikata-san sound so excited.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:19.570
If it isn’t Hajime-kun!

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:20.720
Souji!

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:23.340
Now there’s a face I
haven’t seen in a while!

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:26.890
Oh, Saito!

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:30.580
Hajime-kun? Dang, it’s been ages!

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:34.270
I didn’t think you’d come to Kyoto!

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:36.020
When’d you get here?

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:39.960
It has been a while, hasn’t it?

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:41.490
Got that right!

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:46.510
Hey, Hajime-kun. Since it’s been
a while, why don’t we spar?

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:51.100
Souji here got all blue when you
quit droppin’ by the Shieikan.

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:53.100
Very well, then.

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:54.990
Don’t get carried away.

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:56.570
I know!

00:04:57.170 --> 00:04:59.670
As for Shinpachi, Harada, and Heisuke.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:02.740
Go run a loop patrolling the capital.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:06.350
You sure it’s okay to patrol
the place without permission?

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:09.870
Even if we do eventually manage
to get some clan to sponsor us,

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:12.040
it doesn’t hurt to
stack up some merits.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:14.000
Ah, makes sense.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.280
If the rogue samurai
are too much for you,

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:17.500
why not just kill the scum?

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:19.010
You keep quiet.

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:23.510
Welp, we might as well take
a quick look ’round.

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:34.520
S-Samurai-sama, please show mercy!

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:38.770
Chill, man. We’ll use this money
for the sake of our country.

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:40.770
B-but--

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:46.340
Bastard! Are you sayin’
you can’t help us out

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:48.280
when we’re out workin’ our
butts off for the Emperor?

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:50.620
I-I would never...!

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:54.660
Brat, what’s with that nasty look?

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:56.790
Give back our money, thieves!

00:05:56.950 --> 00:05:58.480
You callin’ us thieves?!

00:05:58.480 --> 00:05:59.540
You damn brat!

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:03.960
Let it drop. He’s just a kid.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:06.720
We won’t go easy on anyone
who insults us warriors,

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:07.800
even if it’s just a kid!

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:10.000
You call yourselves “warriors”

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.180
when you’re raising your
fists to a child and stealing?!

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:13.760
Good point.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:16.440
Since we’re warriors,
usin’ fists don’t cut it.

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:20.670
If you’re a warrior, draw your sword.

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:24.320
What’s keepin’ ya?

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:26.570
That sword on your hip just for show?

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.070
Draw already!

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:41.700
Friggin’ coward.

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:53.300
You okay, Ryunosuke?

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:54.770
Heisuke...?

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:57.190
Shoo!

00:06:57.950 --> 00:06:59.780
Who’re you supposed to be?

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:01.350
Are you TRYING to get in our way?

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:02.310
Beat it!

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:05.750
I’m afraid that ain’t happening.

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:10.950
It’s our job to protect Kyoto
from rogue samurai like you.

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:13.210
“Rogue samurai”? Of all the nerve!

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:29.920
I’m afraid it looks like
that’s the end of the line.

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:42.380
For bein’ such smart asses,

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:44.930
your skills with the sword sure do suck.

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:46.650
Your swords are cryin’!

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:49.660
Damn them!

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:51.780
You okay, Ryunosuke?

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:57.530
That was a close one.

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:01.540
I can get up on my own!

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:11.800
Wasn’t this yours?

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:13.520
What’s wrong?

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:16.720
We’re leaving!

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:17.670
O-okay!

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:24.000
What’s his problem?
It wouldn’t kill him to thank us.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:25.930
What’s all this fuss?

00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:27.710
Rogue samurai were at it again.

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:30.640
They’re such a nuisance!

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:32.820
All they ever do is stir trouble.

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:35.560
I wish they’d leave already!

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:39.110
N-now just a second! We were--

00:08:39.110 --> 00:08:40.690
Let’s go, Heisuke.

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:42.830
B-but Sano-san!

00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:44.770
Forget it. We’re leaving.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:52.840
Let’s go, Ryunosuke.

00:08:53.530 --> 00:08:56.310
Hey, Ryunosuke! Where are you going?

00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:58.000
To buy more SAKE.

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.100
Mibu Temple of the Enmei Jizo Bodhisattva

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:28.630
Most impressive, Hajime-kun.

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:30.590
You don’t let a moment’s
weakness slip by.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:47.080
You’re still the same as ever.

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:48.970
Just the fact that you’re left-handed

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:50.360
makes you all the harder to lunge at.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:52.050
And it would seem you’ve improved upon

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:53.820
your SURI-ASHI slide step as well.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:56.990
I bet you’re going to be unbeatable,
even here in Kyoto.

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:30.820
You got... one in.

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:39.120
Hey, Hajime-kun. Have you
changed the way you lunge?

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:44.030
Did you undergo training at a
different dojo or something?

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:47.040
No, I don’t believe I
have changed my style.

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:56.050
Truly, I am excited that you
rushed to our aid, Saito-kun.

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:57.590
It is most heartening!

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:00.840
With you here, we’re
a hundred men stronger!

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:01.870
Sir!

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:08.240
With him here, everyone from
our Edo days has been reunited.

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:12.030
What’s Ryunosuke up to?

00:11:12.030 --> 00:11:13.740
I told him we’re eating,

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:15.490
but he said he doesn’t want any dinner.

00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:17.450
A moment, Nagakura-kun.

00:11:17.450 --> 00:11:18.110
Yeah?

00:11:18.590 --> 00:11:20.270
How was the city?

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:25.370
Right. I spotted ruffians causin’
problems here and there.

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:29.750
It’d probably be best if we
avoided going out alone.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:33.920
A rogue samurai could
strike us down at any time.

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:35.880
And the locals won’t be of any help.

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:39.760
I see... This is even
worse than I had imagined.

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:42.130
Let them bring it on!

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:45.370
Because the locals and the
clans aren’t up to task,

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:47.510
we’ve got a chance to
make a name for ourselves.

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:50.900
You came prepared for
danger, didn’t you?

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:53.900
You aren’t going to declare
you want to go home to Edo, right?

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:56.200
I wouldn’t a followed ya all the

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:58.400
way to Kyoto if I was gonna do that.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:02.910
Yeah! Everyone here formed
their resolve ages ago!

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:06.060
This may prove trying, but I hope

00:12:06.060 --> 00:12:08.040
you will bear with us for a while!

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:10.790
Don’t even get started, Kondou-san.

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:13.030
We’re used to the poor life!

00:12:13.030 --> 00:12:16.170
Like, seriously. Just gettin’ miso
soup and

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:20.330
pickles is a luxury compared
to life back at the Shieikan.

00:12:20.330 --> 00:12:21.670
You said it!

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:30.680
If you’re a warrior, draw your sword.

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:35.310
What’s keepin’ ya?
That sword on your hip just for show?

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:42.420
Damn it...!

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:58.580
For a lowly dog to sleep
before its master,

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:00.280
you’re doing quite well for yourself.

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:01.710
Serizawa-san...?

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:04.470
Where is my SAKE?

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:07.970
I went and bought you some!

00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:15.010
Can’t complain about that, right?

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:17.840
Even a five-year old child

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:20.480
could accomplish a chore on this level.

00:13:20.990 --> 00:13:23.270
At least you coulda said,
“Job well done.”

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:27.430
I’ll call if I need you.

00:13:27.430 --> 00:13:29.530
Don’t go to bed before your master.

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:38.630
You’re hitting the town
so you can guard him?

00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:43.000
Correct. Today Lord Iemochi
shall enter the capital.

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:46.120
Although we were not called to serve,

00:13:46.120 --> 00:13:50.270
we originally came to the capital
specifically to protect the Shogun.

00:13:51.860 --> 00:13:54.130
Considering the state
of Kyoto these days,

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:56.260
we should go volunteer to guard him.

00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:58.910
There is no need to
guard that inept fool.

00:13:59.970 --> 00:14:03.530
Serizawa-dono, that was out of
line even if said in mere jest!

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:07.030
I simply called him inept because he is.

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:10.180
It is a disgrace to the Shogun line

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:13.050
for nobles who have holed up
here for a thousand years

00:14:13.050 --> 00:14:15.520
to summon him so they can
request he expel the foreigners.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:18.280
Serizawa-sensei, it’s me, Niimi.

00:14:18.550 --> 00:14:19.290
Enter!

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:26.130
I saw him.

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:28.680
Ouch!

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:32.930
That was utterly worthless!
You’re one useless mutt!

00:14:37.070 --> 00:14:37.850
Serizawa-dono!

00:14:39.470 --> 00:14:43.480
If you wish to go, then just the
group of you are free to do so.

00:14:43.910 --> 00:14:45.210
I won’t stop you.

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:48.010
Serizawa-dono!

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:51.350
Let it go, Kondou-san. Just
the lot of us will go.

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:54.670
He said he wouldn’t stop us.

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:57.260
Then that’s all we can do...

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:02.660
Serizawa-san said something
nuts like that?

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:04.090
Yeah...

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:08.640
It looks like that guy
seriously hates our guts.

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:12.840
He must still bear a grudge
over the Honjou Inn incident.

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:13.860
Honjou Inn?

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:16.100
Eh?! Oh, well...

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:17.830
Go ahead and tell him.

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:19.790
Hajime-kun doesn’t
know about it either.

00:15:20.570 --> 00:15:21.490
’Kay.t

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:24.950
When we were traveling to Kyoto
together with Serizawa-san,

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:28.600
Kondou-san was given the job of
“advanced accommodations requisition.”

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:30.630
Advanced accommodations requisition?

00:15:31.020 --> 00:15:32.450
It was his duty to

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:35.490
travel ahead and find
rooms for the Roshigumi.

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:39.300
But he made a booking
error at the Honjou Inn

00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:42.020
and didn’t get a room for Serizawa-san.

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:45.460
Wh-what are you doing, Serizawa-dono?!

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:50.010
Serizawa-san said that it
gets extremely cold at night,

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:53.260
so he trashed a nearby
building and set it afire.

00:15:57.120 --> 00:15:59.660
In the end, Kondou-san got on his

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:02.310
hands and knees and
apologized to Serizawa-san.

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:23.480
Somehow or other we managed to
make it to Kyoto in one piece,

00:16:23.480 --> 00:16:25.510
but it put a rift between us.

00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:27.540
Kondou-san...

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:30.850
Could you please quit acting that way

00:16:30.850 --> 00:16:32.440
around Serizawa-san from now on?

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:35.390
Acting what way?

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:39.030
Calling him “Serizawa-dono” and
trying to read his expressions.

00:16:39.030 --> 00:16:39.930
But...

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:43.200
You stand as Serizawa-san’s equal.

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:45.690
There is no need for you
to feel inferior to him.

00:16:45.930 --> 00:16:48.470
I agree wholeheartedly with Hijikata-kun.

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:53.410
Kondou-san, you are our commander.

00:16:57.740 --> 00:16:58.830
Very well.

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:12.640
This is stinkin’ crowded!

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:14.530
We’d never know if there
were any rogue samurai

00:17:14.530 --> 00:17:16.170
mingling amongst all these people!

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:18.260
Don’t you need to be closer up?

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:19.820
Yeah, you’re right.

00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:22.800
We can’t protect no one
worth squat from back here!

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:24.130
Oh, he’s here!

00:17:24.130 --> 00:17:25.850
The Shogun is passing through!

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:30.580
AMBITION

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:38.480
Let us through!

00:17:38.480 --> 00:17:42.590
The Roshigumi has come to
guard Lord Shogun Iemochi!

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:53.170
H-hey!

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:14.270
So this is what it will take for
the Bakufu to sponsor us...

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:35.130
Lord Iemochi... The Shogun...

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:36.710
is right there!

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:39.910
Isn’t this great, Kondou-san?

00:18:40.210 --> 00:18:41.640
Uh-huh...!

00:18:42.150 --> 00:18:45.880
Next time we will guard
Lord Iemochi up close,

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:48.640
not from amidst the crowd of onlookers!

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:51.290
You’re right! We will!

00:18:58.800 --> 00:19:00.730
Niimi, what say you?

00:19:01.330 --> 00:19:05.710
This will play a big role in
freeing us of our current situation.

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:10.240
Serizawa-sensei, please leave this to me.

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:15.670
MIBU TEMPLE

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:33.440
Yo!

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:36.440
Knock it off!

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:38.200
C’mon! C’mon over.

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:41.940
Now then, Ryunosuke,
let’s practice together.

00:19:41.940 --> 00:19:44.090
I have to go shopping, so I’ll pass.

00:19:44.090 --> 00:19:47.150
Did Serizawa-san send you
out to buy some more SAKE?

00:19:47.150 --> 00:19:49.710
I’m amazed you don’t get sick of
that crap day in and day out.

00:19:50.050 --> 00:19:51.580
I’m getting tobacco today!

00:19:58.050 --> 00:20:01.090
It’s dangerous out there.
Want me to go with you?

00:20:01.390 --> 00:20:03.840
I’m not a kid! I can go by myself!

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:05.460
Hey, now...

00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:06.460
Leave him be.

00:20:08.530 --> 00:20:10.870
If he wants to die, let him go die.

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:15.860
It’s not like I want
to die or anything.

00:20:16.240 --> 00:20:19.090
You aren’t skilled with the sword,
nor do you train.

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:20.800
You can’t even draw your sword

00:20:20.800 --> 00:20:22.610
when someone directs his at you.

00:20:23.520 --> 00:20:25.780
Despite all of that, you put on the

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:27.570
tough act and pick fights with samurai.

00:20:27.930 --> 00:20:29.620
Dammit, Heisuke...

00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:33.260
You can’t blame me for
thinking you are eager to die.

00:20:33.260 --> 00:20:34.470
Back at you!

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:36.910
You came to Kyoto knowing that you could

00:20:36.910 --> 00:20:38.500
get killed by some rogue samurai!

00:20:38.770 --> 00:20:40.680
That looks like a death wish to--

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:45.450
Don’t lump people trying
to accomplish something

00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:47.140
with someone racing to his death!

00:20:48.340 --> 00:20:50.280
I-I’m not...

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:53.980
At the very least, you aren’t
desperately fighting to live.

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:56.640
If you don’t want to die,

00:20:56.640 --> 00:21:00.150
throw sand or mud in your
enemy’s face and run!

00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:10.860
That’s the only way he knows
how to express himself.

00:21:10.860 --> 00:21:14.370
That’s his way of showing
he’s worried about you.

00:21:23.910 --> 00:21:28.680
Jeez, why do I have to handle
the cleaning out here too?

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:35.690
Yuu-boy, what’s wrong?

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:37.860
I’m scared!

00:21:37.860 --> 00:21:39.630
Who’s that kid?

00:21:39.770 --> 00:21:41.130
He lives here.

00:23:31.090 --> 00:23:32.710
“Rules of Conduct,” eh?

00:23:32.710 --> 00:23:36.100
I’m amazed you were able to
come up with something like this.

00:23:36.100 --> 00:23:37.940
The only way to keep the crowd in check

00:23:37.940 --> 00:23:40.480
is to clamp down on
them with strict rules.

00:23:40.480 --> 00:23:42.650
Violators must commit honorable suicide.

00:23:42.650 --> 00:23:44.650
RULES FOR A PACK
OF WOLVES

00:23:43.050 --> 00:23:44.170
Isn’t that right?
